# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF line endings, on every operating system.
# Git for Windows converts to CRLF on checkout by default; the checker's git (Linux, inside the container)
# would then see every file as modified, and `itsmlab verify` would report the commit as "(dirty)".
# LF also keeps shell scripts and Dockerfiles you add working inside Linux containers.
* text=auto eol=lf
